      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "SILVER SEQUINS (8) sizzled around 410m in 23.12 when winning a Grade 5 at Horsham last start. Rates a top chance again if runs up to latest. WHY NOT SEB (1) flew the lids from out wide with an impressive turn of foot before finishing third (24.94) and beaten 2.75 lengths over 435m at Sale. Expecting another good run. CRACKERJACK KEV (2) was safely held last time out, finishing seventh at Traralgon over 425m behind Maximum Sunset (24.62) in a Grade 5. Was in the money prior to that. Has a strong record out of this box with three wins and a minor placing from five starts. Has ability and can measure up. QUICK SHOT (5) cannot be left out despite racing here for the first time.",
